+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Stack (confirmed by user)
+- language: JavaScript, vanilla, no framework, no preprocessors, no build step.
+- persistence: vanilla localStorage.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanilla`, from the `todos-[framework]` format in `assets/app-spec.md`.
+- routing: hash routes `#/`, `#/active`, `#/completed`. `assets/app-spec.md` offers Flatiron Director from `/assets`, but `assets/` carries no `director.js`, so the vanilla build implements a custom hashchange router. Behaviour specs are mechanism-agnostic.
+
+## Greenfield fast path not yet run
+- `RIGGING.md` absent. Next cycle runs the fast-path bootstrap: discover the five required values, offer the Node quality toolchain, install the harness runner and confirmed tools, write minimal `RIGGING.md`, then dispatch QM.
+- `README.md` already states runner = `cucumber-js`, specs dir = `features`, step defs = `features/support`.
+- `package.json` devDependencies: `@cucumber/cucumber`, `happy-dom`, both at `"*"`. Pin to concrete versions at bootstrap per `locked` dependency policy.
+- Verification tier: Voyage 1 opens on the cheapest tier that observes the DOM behaviour. `happy-dom` is installed and is the named cheapest tier for a Node stack rendering a DOM; adopt `happy-dom` unless a behaviour cannot be observed below a real-browser tier, and then record that as a named decision.
+
+## Dependencies to install at bootstrap (product, mandated by assets/app-spec.md)
+- `todomvc-common` (`base.css`, `base.js` referenced by `assets/app-template.index.html`).
+- `todomvc-app-css` (`index.css` referenced by `assets/app-template.index.html`).
+- Not present in `node_modules` now. Install at bootstrap and record under `RIGGING.md` `## Dependencies`.
+
+## Spec scope notes (Captain calls)
+- DOM classes that carry product meaning (`completed`, `editing`, `selected`) are asserted as observable states via product-named steps; raw CSS selectors stay out of scenario text and land in step definitions.
+- The destroy button's hover-reveal is a CSS behaviour in `todomvc-app-css` and is not observable in the `happy-dom` tier, so no scenario pins it; the click-removes behaviour covers the destroy control.
+- The `id` format is not pinned; only its presence and uniqueness are specified.
+
+## Open questions for the user
+1. Routing library: ship a custom vanilla hashchange router (current spec path), or add Flatiron Director as a dependency? Director is not present in `assets/`.
+2. Quality toolchain for the fast-path offer: confirm `gplint` (feature lint) + `biome` (code lint/format) + `c8` (coverage) + `jsdoc -X` (plank inventory on plain JavaScript)? Or decline any?
+3. Pin `@cucumber/cucumber` and `happy-dom` to concrete versions at bootstrap.
diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
