+++ b/features/new-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: New todo
+  As a person with things to do
+  I want to add a todo by typing and pressing Enter
+  So that I can capture what needs to be done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is freshly loaded with no todos
+
+  Rule: The new-todo input is ready when the page loads
+
+  Scenario: The new-todo input is focused on initial render
+    Then the new-todo input has focus
+
+  Rule: Enter creates a todo from the trimmed, non-empty input
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Enter creates a todo from the input text
+    When I enter "Buy milk" in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo
+    And the todo list shows the todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed from a new todo
+    When I enter "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list shows the todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: The new-todo input is cleared after a todo is created
+    When I enter "Buy milk" in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    Then the new-todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: A blank input does not create a todo
+    When I enter "   " in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list shows 0 todos
+
+  Scenario: New todos are appended to the end of the list in entry order
+    When I enter "Buy milk" in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    And I enter "Walk the dog" in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    Then the todo list shows 2 todos
+    And the todo list shows the todos in the order "Buy milk", "Walk the dog"
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0fa2ee8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+Feature: Persistence to localStorage
+  As a person returning to the app
+  I want my todos to persist in localStorage
+  So that I do not lose my list when the page reloads
+
+  Rule: Todos persist under the project localStorage key in the documented shape
+
+  Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage under the key "todos-vanilla"
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    Then localStorage holds the key "todos-vanilla"
+    And the value of the "todos-vanilla" key is a JSON array with 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Each persisted todo has the keys id, title, and completed
+    Given the todo app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then every item in the "todos-vanilla" localStorage key has the keys "id", "title", and "completed"
+
+  Scenario: A completed todo is persisted with completed set to true
+    Given the todo app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is marked as complete
+    Then the persisted todo "Buy milk" has completed set to true
+
+  Scenario: Persisted todo ids are unique
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    Then the ids in the "todos-vanilla" localStorage key are unique
+
+  Rule: Every change persists dynamically
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo updates localStorage
+    Given the todo app is freshly loaded with no todos
+    When I enter "Buy milk" in the new-todo input
+    And I press the Enter key in the new-todo input
+    Then the value of the "todos-vanilla" key is a JSON array with 1 item
+
+  Scenario: Destroying a todo updates localStorage
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When I click the destroy button of the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the value of the "todos-vanilla" key is a JSON array with 1 item
+
+  Rule: Editing mode is not persisted
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted to localStorage
+    Given the todo app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the page reloads
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
+    And the todo list shows the todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Todos are restored on reload
+
+  Scenario: Todos are restored from localStorage on reload
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the page reloads
+    Then the todo list shows 2 todos
+    And the todo list shows the todos in the order "Buy milk", "Walk the dog"
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..be687e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a person focusing on part of my list
+  I want to filter todos by their state through the URL
+  So that I can view all, active, or completed todos
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk", "Walk the dog", and "Feed the cat"
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is marked as complete
+
+  Rule: Each route filters the visible todos
+
+  Scenario: The All route shows every todo
+    Given the route is "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 3 todos
+    And the All filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: A blank route defaults to all todos
+    Given the route is blank
+    Then the todo list shows 3 todos
+    And the All filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    Given the route is "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 todos
+    And the todo list shows the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list does not show the todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the Active filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the route is "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo
+    And the todo list shows the todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo list does not show the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the Completed filter link is selected
+
+  Rule: A todo that no longer matches the filter is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo in the active filter hides it
+    Given the route is "#/active"
+    When I check the toggle of the todo "Feed the cat"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 todo
+    And the todo list does not show the todo "Feed the cat"
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a todo in the completed filter hides it
+    Given the route is "#/completed"
+    When I uncheck the toggle of the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the todo list shows 0 todos
+
+  Rule: The active filter persists across reload
+
+  Scenario: The active filter is restored on reload
+    Given the route is "#/active"
+    When the page reloads
+    Then the route is "#/active"
+    And the Active filter link is selected
+    And the todo list shows 2 todos
diff --git a/features/visibility.feature b/features/visibility.feature
